                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "25669465",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198034463222",
                            "num_reviews": 6,
                            "playtime_forever": 294,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 294,
                            "last_played": 1474737029
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've only played the first two acts (out of five), but here's what I thought of it so far:\n\n* Everything that touches you kills you instantly, which adds to the challenge.\n\n* On the other hand, enemies also die with one shot (except for bosses).\n\n* There are checkpoints every now and then. They look pretty awesome and are quite useful.\n\n* It seems the level designs is inspired by Sonic levels, i.e. you have multiple paths, which is good. There are timerun challenges and collection challenges.\n\n* You start with 15 lives. When you run out of lives, you start in the town again. You can visit the second house and jump into any acts that you've visited.\n\n* I played with a PS3 controller. The controls have a good amount of weight to them, but I wish the shooting had a bit less of a delay between shots.\n\n* I wish there were upgrades or power ups to spice things up.\n\n* Animations are cute and detailed. The world in general has been crafted with love.\n\n* Music is okay. Sound could use a bit more work, I think, but it does the job.\n\n* Bosses are HARD. Especially the second one, because it summons worms all over the place. And worms jump at you in random directions.\n\n* I hate those worms. :D\n\n* Framerate is super smooth and I have everything set to ultra.\n\n* One thing I'd change: I pressed L2 accidentally, which resets your progress in the current act! A confirmation popup of some sort would be helpful.\n\nGive it a try, if you like a challenging old-school platformer. (:",
